      "seed": 1263561627,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1202398891,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795550704984,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Monte Carlo error  ∝  1/√N\n\nTo get 10× smaller error:\n  need 100× more samples (√100 = 10 ✓)\n\nFrom the notebook (π estimation):\n  N =    10,000,000  →  error ≈ 0.00032\n  N = 1,000,000,000  →  error ≈ 0.00003\n                        (1 extra decimal)\n\nFor option pricing in Q17:\n  2 → 4 correct dp needs\n  10,000  →  100,000,000 paths!\n\nThis is why we use:\n  · Antithetic variates\n  · Control variates\n  · Quasi-Monte Carlo",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Monte Carlo error  ∝  1/√N\n\nTo get 10× smaller error:\n  need 100× more samples (√100 = 10 ✓)\n\nFrom the notebook (π estimation):\n  N =    10,000,000  →  error ≈ 0.00032\n  N = 1,000,000,000  →  error ≈ 0.00003\n                        (1 extra decimal)\n\nFor option pricing in Q17:\n  2 → 4 correct dp needs\n  10,000  →  100,000,000 paths!\n\nThis is why we use:\n  · Antithetic variates\n  · Control variates\n  · Quasi-Monte Carlo",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
