    {
      "id": "qn038",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 166,
      "y": 970,
      "width": 1310,
      "height": 81.25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ac",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1878946392,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1494791616,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795550704984,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Assumes stock follows GBM.  Option price  =  E[ max(S_T − K, 0) ] × e^(−rT)\nMonte Carlo approach (Q17): simulate many GBM paths → compute payoff on each → average → option price.\n1/√N means 4 decimal places of accuracy requires ~100M paths — extremely slow.\nBlack-Scholes derived a closed-form solution, eliminating Monte Carlo for vanilla options entirely.\nExotic / path-dependent options (barriers, Asians) still need Monte Carlo because no closed form exists.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Assumes stock follows GBM.  Option price  =  E[ max(S_T − K, 0) ] × e^(−rT)\nMonte Carlo approach (Q17): simulate many GBM paths → compute payoff on each → average → option price.\n1/√N means 4 decimal places of accuracy requires ~100M paths — extremely slow.\nBlack-Scholes derived a closed-form solution, eliminating Monte Carlo for vanilla options entirely.\nExotic / path-dependent options (barriers, Asians) still need Monte Carlo because no closed form exists.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
